        "id": 2705190082,
        "content": "No I don't think I follow your logic. \n- Let's say I rotate the private key. \n- I place it into the secrets so the kernel can use it. \n- The new public key can be derived from the private key. \n- The public key is hosted on a public api endpoint. \n- All systems relying on the key should fetch the public key. \nOptionally they can re encrypt at run time?",
